      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test is heavily bloated with dead code — fields and methods using an undefined type parameter `E`, unused utility methods copied from an abstract test base class — while the actual test logic is only at the bottom. I'll write a clean, self-contained version.Now let me compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes ~400 lines of dead code (unused fields with undefined type parameter `E`, copied-but-unused base-class utility methods) and replaces them with a clean, self-contained test: a private `IntegerTransformer` nested class, minimal `resetEmpty`/`resetFull`/`verify` helpers, and the test method itself structured with clear scenario comments explaining each `removeIf` case."
